      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T22:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It assumes 64 byte cache lines. When the width is a multiple of 128 values, a 2 row step is a multiple of 2 * 128 * 4 \u003d 1024 bytes. Each read of a column then lands 16 lines after the previous one, so only every 16th set gets used. A bigger power of 2 in the width makes it worse. At 2560 the step is 5 x 4 KB, and a column uses 1 of every 64 sets.",
      "parentUuid": "a215f2ce_ad381078",
      "revId": "978dc959d997f6886d22da561fdfe086e43558dc",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
